From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: B Honey <9922368+Mhsbrian@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] OPENBOOK: arm64: emulate MRS of the ID registers as Linux
 does

A real arm64 kernel traps EL0 reads of MIDR_EL1, MPIDR_EL1, REVIDR_EL1 and the
ID_AA64* feature registers (op0=3, op1=0, CRn=0, CRm 0 or 2..7) and returns
sanitised values, and says so with HWCAP_CPUID. Here only MIDR_EL1 was
handled; every other ID register raised SIGILL. Go's golang.org/x/sys/cpu reads
ID_AA64ISAR0_EL1, ID_AA64ISAR1_EL1 and ID_AA64PFR0_EL1 when it cannot read
/proc/self/auxv, which Android apps cannot, so every gomobile library died at
load (Tor VPN: SIGILL at mrs x0, id_aa64isar0_el1).

guest_id_registers_arm64.h now holds the guest CPU identity: AT_HWCAP and the
ID register values, built like arm64_ftr_reg_user_value() (visible fields from
the features the guest has, hidden fields at the kernel's safe value, untracked
registers RAZ). The interpreter and the lite translator return them; the heavy
tier still leaves these regions to the lite tier. AT_HWCAP gains HWCAP_CPUID,
which the emulated /proc/cpuinfo already listed.
